#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
Wrapper to run Codex review from within Claude Code.
Claude Code should call this via Bash, NOT review code/plans itself.

Usage:
    codex-review                    # code review (last commit)
    codex-review --arch             # architecture review
    codex-review --commit abc123    # review specific commit
    codex-review --unpushed         # review all unpushed commits vs origin
    codex-review --print-model      # print the configured review model/effort and exit
    codex-review --pin abc123       # review INSIDE a temp worktree pinned at SHA
                                    # (HEAD-drift-safe in shared/multi-session repos;
                                    #  worktree is created and cleaned up automatically)

Runtime: internal watchdog TIMEOUT=2400s (override: CODEX_REVIEW_TIMEOUT env, seconds;
raise it for large diffs). Callers (Claude Code Bash tool) must NOT set a
smaller outer timeout — run in background and wait for completion instead (a 5-min outer
timeout killed a healthy review mid-run, real fail 2026-07-11).
Model overrides: CODEX_REVIEW_MODEL and CODEX_REVIEW_EFFORT (empty values are ignored).
Reviews use the user's Codex home and configuration. The wrapper turns off the
plugins, apps, agent_message_board_mcp, and skill_mcp_dependency_install features
with `-c features.<name>=false`, which lets older Codex versions ignore unknown
features. Codex creates the message-board server when a session starts with
multi_agent_v2 and omits it from the listing. A skill mentioned during review can
otherwise install an MCP server into the user's configuration. The wrapper
encodes each enabled server name as a quoted TOML key in a single
`-c mcp_servers=` inline table because separate overrides replace each other.
The review starts only after Codex confirms that no listed server is enabled
and each feature switched off is either disabled or absent from a non-empty feature list.
The wrapper reports cyber_policy refusals and prints a manual Daybreak Blue
command for commit and architecture reviews. It never runs Daybreak itself.
CODEX_REVIEW_DAYBREAK_MODEL and CODEX_REVIEW_DAYBREAK_EFFORT configure the printed command.
"""

